# gettext, target sysroot: every build for the image
### The lib-link macros of gnulib (AC_LIB_LINKFLAGS) look for lib<name>.so in the libdir of the prefix
### with test -f, on the file system of the build host: /usr/lib64 of the host, whose libraries a host of
### the machine of the target links (-L/usr/lib64 -lxml2 -lncurses on generic-x64, libxml2.so.2 in the
### image). Without the search a library is a plain -l<name>, which the compiler finds in the sysroot
CONF_FLAGS+=" --without-libxml2-prefix --without-libncurses-prefix --without-libtermcap-prefix"
CONF_FLAGS+=" --without-libcurses-prefix --without-libxcurses-prefix --without-libunistring-prefix"
CONF_FLAGS+=" --without-libiconv-prefix --without-libintl-prefix --without-libtextstyle-prefix"
